1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
Twelve people asleep behind frosted glass, one switch,

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:06,537
and a note that says don't.

3
00:00:08,337 --> 00:00:12,685
Three of my crew are standing in front of it,

4
00:00:13,135 --> 00:00:17,917
and whichever button they press, the ship gets a different quest.

5
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:23,600
This is the checkpoint for the first half of the class.

6
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:30,137
You'll plan one away scene on paper, type it, check it, and play it.

7
00:00:31,337 --> 00:00:33,511
Before any rooms, three sentences.

8
00:00:34,411 --> 00:00:36,585
The question the scene asks.

9
00:00:37,035 --> 00:00:41,383
Why is this hulk drifting, with nobody at the controls?

10
00:00:42,283 --> 00:00:45,761
The answer, which the party finds in pieces.

11
00:00:46,211 --> 00:00:51,863
Her crew put themselves to sleep, to wait for help that never came.

12
00:00:52,763 --> 00:00:56,241
And the choice they make at the end.

13
00:00:56,691 --> 00:01:01,039
Wake them now, or leave them and fetch a doctor.

14
00:01:02,839 --> 00:01:06,317
The pieces of the answer become your readings,

15
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:09,811
and the choice becomes your two endings.

16
00:01:10,711 --> 00:01:13,754
If you can't write the third sentence,

17
00:01:14,204 --> 00:01:17,683
you have a tour, and not a scene.

18
00:01:18,883 --> 00:01:21,926
Next, how much of everything. Six places.

19
00:01:22,376 --> 00:01:26,289
Three readings, one for each job on my roster.

20
00:01:26,739 --> 00:01:30,217
One reading for a skill, and one check.

21
00:01:30,667 --> 00:01:35,450
Five facts in all, and a door that asks for three.

22
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:41,598
Then I draw it, with one room in the middle,

23
00:01:42,048 --> 00:01:45,961
and every other place leads back to that room.

24
00:01:46,861 --> 00:01:51,209
The way home goes in the room they arrive in,

25
00:01:51,659 --> 00:01:54,702
and at each ending, and nowhere else.

26
00:01:55,902 --> 00:01:58,946
This is the table that saves you.

27
00:01:59,846 --> 00:02:04,628
For every fact I write where it is, who's offered it,

28
00:02:05,078 --> 00:02:06,817
and whether it's sure.

29
00:02:08,617 --> 00:02:12,965
A fact is sure when every party can get it.

30
00:02:13,865 --> 00:02:18,213
A reading for a job on my roster is sure,

31
00:02:18,663 --> 00:02:22,141
because when that person stays home, somebody covers.

32
00:02:23,041 --> 00:02:25,650
A reading for a skill isn't,

33
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:29,143
and neither is anything behind a roll.

34
00:02:30,943 --> 00:02:33,117
I have three sure facts.

35
00:02:33,567 --> 00:02:37,915
So my door may ask for three, and no more.

36
00:02:39,115 --> 00:02:45,202
Now I type, in layers, and I run lint after each one. Places first,

37
00:02:45,652 --> 00:02:50,000
and I've torn out my practice rooms to make space.

38
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:53,074
Lint warns about two signals,

39
00:02:53,524 --> 00:03:00,915
and it's right, because the rooms that sent them are gone. Then the readings. Then the check.

40
00:03:01,365 --> 00:03:08,757
Then the door, with a line that tells an early party why it's shut. Then the endings.

41
00:03:09,207 --> 00:03:13,554
Each ending is a quest the ship doesn't have yet,

42
00:03:14,004 --> 00:03:18,352
a choice that starts it, with the new word accepts,

43
00:03:18,802 --> 00:03:22,280
and a last room with one way out.

44
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,820
Then the two stories.

45
00:03:26,270 --> 00:03:28,009
And lint is clean.

46
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:31,817
One change to the ship's quest.

47
00:03:32,717 --> 00:03:37,065
Last time, it waited for the surgeon's story to finish.

48
00:03:37,515 --> 00:03:42,733
But a story is handed to nobody when its person stays home,

49
00:03:43,183 --> 00:03:46,661
so a short crew could never complete it.

50
00:03:48,461 --> 00:03:51,939
Now it waits for the reading's own signal.

51
00:03:52,839 --> 00:03:57,622
The surgeon's press finishes her story and the ship's quest together,

52
00:03:58,072 --> 00:04:03,289
and when she's not there, the covered reading still finishes the ship's.

53
00:04:04,489 --> 00:04:07,967
Lint has passed, and lint checks your spelling.

54
00:04:08,417 --> 00:04:11,026
It doesn't walk through your rooms.

55
00:04:11,926 --> 00:04:14,535
So I do, with a pencil.

56
00:04:16,335 --> 00:04:20,683
One: every room has a way out with no condition.

57
00:04:21,583 --> 00:04:24,626
Two: every room has a way in.

58
00:04:25,526 --> 00:04:30,309
Three: the door asks for no more than the sure facts,

59
00:04:30,759 --> 00:04:33,802
and every fact has its own name.

60
00:04:35,602 --> 00:04:37,776
Four is the big one.

61
00:04:38,226 --> 00:04:43,009
I cross out everything that needs a skill or a roll,

62
00:04:43,459 --> 00:04:47,372
and with what's left I walk to each ending.

63
00:04:48,272 --> 00:04:50,880
If I can, every crew can.

64
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:56,159
Five: each story's reading belongs to its person,

65
00:04:56,609 --> 00:04:59,217
and each ending's quest starts hidden.

66
00:05:00,417 --> 00:05:05,200
Then I play it three times, with a watch beside me.

67
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:07,839
Alone, I'm the chief,

68
00:05:08,289 --> 00:05:12,202
and two readings come to me marked as covering.

69
00:05:13,102 --> 00:05:16,580
Sixteen presses, and I'm home with an ending.

70
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:20,989
With everyone aboard, nothing is covered,

71
00:05:21,439 --> 00:05:24,048
and reading it all takes twenty.

72
00:05:25,848 --> 00:05:28,022
And once, I walk away.

73
00:05:28,472 --> 00:05:30,646
One press in the airlock,

74
00:05:31,096 --> 00:05:35,443
and the visit is over for everybody, with nothing finished.

75
00:05:36,343 --> 00:05:40,257
That's why the way home is where it is.

76
00:05:41,457 --> 00:05:43,196
Now write your own.

77
00:05:44,096 --> 00:05:48,443
Three sentences, a beat sheet, a drawing, a facts table,

78
00:05:48,893 --> 00:05:50,633
and then the typing.

79
00:05:51,533 --> 00:05:53,272
Do the five checks,

80
00:05:53,722 --> 00:06:01,113
and break it three times on purpose, to see lint say clean when the scene is wrong.

81
00:06:02,913 --> 00:06:06,391
Then play it with everyone you can find,

82
00:06:06,841 --> 00:06:09,885
and write down how long it took.
